  {
    "id": "anno-takato_upper_p132_right-03",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "但老幼幷役員兵隊其外總テ之豫備臨時助役等申付候）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "但し、老幼並びに役員・兵隊その外、総て之を予備・臨時助役等に申し付け候"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Qualifying note: the aged and the young, together with officials, troops and everyone else, are all assigned to reserve duty and temporary auxiliary service. It attaches to the exemption count in the column to its right and, like that count, belongs to Takashima. The vertical closing parenthesis at the foot of the column closes a bracket opened on printed page 237, where a marginal note records that the seven lines it encloses were written in red in the original; this is the last of those seven lines."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "高島但書"
      }
    ],
